{"id": "tea:paingala-upanisad:1", "source": "src:paingala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Paiṅgala, after twelve years' service, asks Yājñavalkya; from the witness with māyā arise the avyakta (Īśvara), mahat (Hiraṇyagarbha) and ahaṃkāra (Virāṭ); by quintuplication the gross elements and the world.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "teachers": ["tch:paingala", "tch:yajnavalkya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text paingala-upanisad 1"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text chapter (adhyāya, khaṇḍa or section) 1 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'atha ha paiṅgalo yājñavalkyamupasametya dvādaśavarṣaśuśrūṣāpūrvakaṃ paramarahasya-kaivalyamanubrūhīti…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
